messages:
Eli M: FYI - reproduced a tiny duplicated fragment at the start of resumed SSE streams in our browser polyfill after auth rotation. Looks like 3-6 chars from the previous chunk get replayed.

Harper J: Polyfill only or native EventSource too? Which browsers?

Eli M: Polyfill on Chrome + iOS webviews. Native EventSource doesn't show it. Steps: start stream, wait for short JWT to expire, SDK refresh reconnects, resumed payload begins with a 4-char overlap then continues.

Sofia R: That sounds like the in-memory parse buffer surviving a reconnect while the server resumes inclusively. Do you still keep a partial buffer across reconnects?

Eli M: Yup. Simplified loop:
```
let buf = '';
poly.ondata = chunk => {
  buf += chunk;
  const parts = buf.split('\n\n');
  buf = parts.pop() || '';
  for (const p of parts) handleEvent(p);
};
// reconnect currently preserves buf
```

Harper J: If buf survives and server re-sends overlapping bytes, overlap is inevitable. Quick mitigation: clear buf on reconnect. Longer term: standardize resume semantics to exclusive offsets and add client dedupe by seq id.

ops-bot: note - staging nginx proxy_read_timeout=60s; mid-chunk closes observed under stress which increases chance of fragments.

Sofia R: Agreed. Proposed immediate fixes: (1) clear parse buffer on reconnect in the polyfill, (2) add an SDK option resumePreference: "exclusive"|"inclusive" (default "exclusive"), (3) client-side dedupe by event sequence number.

Harper J: Also recommend server-side keepalive heartbeats like ":hb\n\n" every 15-30s to avoid proxy idle kills. Make sure heartbeats are ignored by the renderer and not billed. Ops should provide an nginx example.

Eli M: I'll open a small PR to clear the buffer on reconnect, add the resumePreference opt-in, and include a unit test that simulates a mid-chunk TCP close. Filing issue #4557 with traces and a minimal repro.

Sofia R: For parity, both Node and browser SDKs should accept Last-Event-ID header and resume_token query param. Also add a short-term fallback: if resume fails >3 times, switch conversation to short-polling so UI doesn't show duplicate diffs.

ci-bot: started CI for branch fix/polyfill-reconnect-overlap (build 10321) :rocket:

Harper J: Action items:
- Eli: PR to clear buffer on reconnect + resumePreference + tests and e2e
- Sofia: spec doc for header/query parity and client dedupe behavior
- Ops: nginx config + keepalive guidance and verify heartbeats not counted for usage

Eli M: Thanks  will tag reviewers. Will close when CI + e2e pass. :white_check_mark:
